[Seven Great Powers: Refers to the seven strongest warriors in the world, a selection of seven people that came to exist following the end of the Second Human-Demon War.

History:
1. Establishment: When the Second Great Human-Demon War came to a conclusion, a person known as the Technique God came up with the name. At that time, Technique God was considered to be one of the strongest people in the world. Technique God selected six more people and declared them to be the strongest in the world.
2. Post-Laplace War: The title of the Seven Great Powers was well known until the Laplace War. All original Seven Powers participated in the Laplace War, with the exception of Technique God. Among them, three were killed, one went missing, and another was sealed away. The Dragon God was the only one who came out of the War with a definite living-status. After hundred of years, with those at the bottom swapping spots and the top four having unknown status to the people, the title fell out of use.
3. Monuments: In order to spread the name of the seven strongest across the world, stone monuments were scattered around the world in places where mana concentration was high. The monument is of knee-height and a single character "7" is inscribed at the middle in the Fighting God language. The seven respective motifs of the Great Power surround the "7" character starting with the rank one motif being situated above the "7" character then sequentially going clockwise are the rest of the Great Power's motif. The stone automatically updates itself when a new Power enters the ranks with their respective motif.

The Seven Great Powers (Rank, Title, Holder, Status):
1st. - Technique God - Laplace (Missing);
2nd. - Dragon God - Orsted (Active);
3rd. - Fighting God - Badigadi (Missing);
4th. - Demon God - Laplace (Inactive, Sealed);
5th. - Death God - Randolph Marianne (Active);
6th. - Sword God - Gal Farion (Active);
7th. - North God - Aleksander Rybak (Active).

Trivia:
- It was believed the Technique God created this system so that he could find people capable of defeating him.
- After the Laplace War, people began to doubt whether the Technique God even really existed at all.
- Even though the Seven Power holders are said to be the absolute strongest of the world, there is further division within the group. The first four ranks (1-4) are referred as the "upper" ranks and the remaining three ranks (5-7) are referred to as the "lower" ranks. There is a very large difference in strength between the fourth (Demon God) and the fifth (Death God).
- The ranking only changes when someone on the ranking is defeated or dead. As a result, the ranks are not directly correlated to their combat prowess. For example: The Technique God holds the #1 position despite Orsted being stronger, because he is missing and not defeated.
- Prior to Demon Dragon King Laplace being split into two different beings, the Seven Great Powers ranking system had not yet been established. As such, Laplace as the Demon Dragon King is not part of the Seven Great Powers, yet takes two separate seats as two different beings after the creation of the ranking system.]

[About Laplace Factor: A unique trait in capability, or sometimes bodily appearance, a rare percentage of people are born with. It is a result of the Demon God Laplace sending his soul from the past into the present by having it attached itself to multiple bodies in preparation of his revival.

Some characteristics of people with a Laplace Factor:
- Increased magic potential and capacity (in most cases);
- Green hair (some cases);
- Can't wear or have trouble wearing Battle Aura (most cases);
- Increased strength and endurance;
- When entering Perugius' Castle, they emit light particles out of their bodies (all cases).

Origin: Approximately 400 years prior to the start of the story, when Demon God Laplace was defeated and sealed by the, presently-known, Three Legendary Demon-God Slayers he initiated a reincarnation method by which he would reincarnate in the far future. This method of reincarnation involves sending the soul of oneself into the future and plant itself onto multiple people to search for the perfect vessel. Those said people would have unique traits, though mostly dormant, originally associated with Laplace's internal or physical features. When those people give birth to children, Laplace's traits they inherited will be passed down to their offspring. As a result, slight bodily changes start to appear in children.
The process of bodies adapting to the soul would repeat for numerous generations, and slowly, when Laplace's predicted time of reincarnation gets closer, the dormant traits starts to awaken signaling the body-adaptation is getting nearer to the ideal. By this point in time, the person in possession of the factor would have already noticed their abnormality, by intuition or when exhibited for any person to notice. It must be noted that the traits awaken in different persons possessing the factor.
The reincarnation will occur when an adapted body possessing the factor perfectly matches with the soul. Taking over the body of the soul it was originally supposed to be in and be born while pretending to be it. This was originally a technique of reincarnation perfected by the first generation Dragon God which had been used by many ancient Dragon Race people to reincarnate into the present. Laplace's knowledge of this technique owed to him already having learnt it before he was split from the Demon-Dragon King self; knowledge of this technique was passed to his Demon God self.]

[About curses and blessings: Curses are special powers born from abnormalities in Mana. They can manifest in two forms: users with "beneficial" powers are known as Miko (aka "Blessed Child"), and users with disadvantageous or harmful powers are known as Cursed One (aka "Cursed Child"). However, it is important to note that even Miko powers can sometimes have drawbacks or disadvantages for the user.

Scholars speculate that this suggests a connection between curses and magical items. According to his theory, the effects of curses and magic items are essentially the same.

Curses can come in many forms, here are some examples:
- Being very sexually active to the point of becoming a dangerous sexual beast, and will lead to death if the person is not sexually satiated;
- Being feared by all creatures of the Human World;
- The curse of being unable to go all-out in combat;
Etc.

Examples of blessings:
- Having the trust of all the people in the world;
- To be able to talk to people in their sleep and read their minds in that moment;
- To be able to read people's minds, to one degree or another;
Etc.
Side effects of blessings:
- Being in a dream-like state;
- Not being able to fully control the ability;
Etc.

There are very few people in the world with these gifts and curses. Also, as long as you are not royalty, Miko's birth name will be taken away and you will be forced to work for the kingdom, as a tool in the hands of power.]

[Incantations: The usual length of a magic's Incantation is the higher the rank, the longer the Incantation is. For example, an Elementary Rank Water Magic incantation has only a few sentences while a God Rank Detoxification Spell can be long enough to be in a book as thick as a dictionary.
Some examples of Incantations:
- Healing - "Divine power is rich and nourishing. It offers the strength to rise again to those who have lost their strength. Healing.";
- Water Ball - "Let the great protection of water be on the place thou seekest. I call a refreshing burbling stream here and now. Water Ball.";
- X-Healing - "Oh merciful mother of gods, please heal this one's wounds, and let him recover with a healthy body. X-Healing.";
- Fireball - "Let the great protection of fire be on the place thou seekest. I call the bold heat of a torch here and now. Fireball!";
- Lightning - "O spirits of the magnificent waters, I beseech the Prince of Thunder! Grant me my wish, bless me with thy savagery, and reveal to this insignificant servant a glimpse of thy power! Let fear strike the heart of man as thy divine hammer strikes its anvil and over the land with water! Come, o rain and was everything away in thy flood of destruction!
I call upon you, mighty spirit of light, shining lord of the heavens! Do you see the impudent foe towering before us? Do you see your sown enemy, in all his arrogance? I would be the holy blade that strikes him down! Let your radiant power teach him that the Emperor yet reign supreme! Lightning!";
- Icicle Edge - Truncated Chant: "Majestic blade of ice, I summon thee to strike my enemy down! Icicle Edge!";
- Flame Slice - Truncated Chant: "Take up thy burnt blade and pierce through thy enemy! Flame Slice!".]

[Magic Rank Titles:
1. Beginner/Elementary: Basic mana manipulation;
2. Intermediate: Advanced mana manipulation;
3. Advanced: Complex mana manipulation. Generally large area of effect;
4. Saintly/Holy: Large scale complex mana manipulation. Usually spells that affects the weather;
5. Kingly: Builds upon Saint-class Magic by increasing its effectiveness;
6. Imperial/Emperor: Further enhances the scale of King-class Magic;
7. Divine/God: Continental scale magic.

Spell rankings are typically proportionate to the amount of mana necessary to cast the spell. However, there are exceptions, such as when a person can reach a high rank using lower-ranked magic as a base, i.e. things like skill in using magic, etc. are also deciding factors.
It has been stated that only 1 in 20 people is born with the capacity of using mana and of those, only 1 in 20 is capable of learning how to master it and becoming a mage. However, only 1 in a 100 of those is actually capable of becoming an advanced magician in only 1 element.
The magician's ranking title is determined by the most advanced spell s/he could cast.]

[About Swordsmanship: Due to the influence of the Superd Tribe, spears are said to be weapons of the devil and long-handled weapons are not favored, and bows with limited attack power cannot be used against strong people due to the existence of Battle Aura, so swordsmanship was emphasized and developed.

Three Major Schools: There are three schools of swordsmanship that are mainstream in the human world: Sword God Style, North God Style, Water God Style. Only those who have studied one of the Three Major Schools are called Swordsmen; in other schools, even if they use a sword, they are not called Swordsmen but Warriors.

All three schools have seven ranks:
1. Elementary Rank;
2. Intermediate Rank;
3. Advanced Rank;
4. Holy Rank;
5. Royal Rank;
6. Imperial Rank;
7. Divine Rank.

At the Intermediate Rank, they have the power to compete with ordinary knights, at the Holy Rank, they are called geniuses, and at the Royal Rank and above, they are considered to be among the most talented in the world.]
